    "created_at": "2022-01-15T01:28:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-15T01:28:38Z",
    "body": "On Git Bash one cannot create directories under `/usr/` as it is locked, instead a different location should be used, as @davidkna suggests.\r\n\r\nI did the following.\r\n\r\n1. Run\r\n    ```bash\r\n    $ cd ~\r\n    $ mkdir -p .starship/bin\r\n    ```\r\n1. Install Starship\r\n    ```bash\r\n    sh -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://starship.rs/install.sh)\" -- --bin-dir=\"$HOME/.starship/bin/\"\r\n    ```\r\n1. And for upgrading I created a simple bash file called `starship-upgrade.sh` sitting on my `$HOME` directory with the same command from the previous step\r\n    ```bash\r\n    #!/usr/bin/bash\r\n    \r\n    sh -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://starship.rs/install.sh)\" -- --bin-dir=\"$HOME/.starship/bin/\"\r\n    ```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
